        </p>
      </aside>

      <section aria-labelledby="where-to-start">
        <h2 id="where-to-start">Where To Start</h2>

        <p>Most readers do not begin with Patterns or Lenses.</p>

        <p>They begin with a problem.</p>

        <p>
          Start with <a href="/workbench/check-input/">Check Input</a> when you
          have an input you are about to give an AI system.
        </p>

        <p>
          Start with <a href="/workbench/issues/">Issues</a> when you want to
          browse visible failure surfaces.
        </p>

        <p>
          Start with <a href="/workbench/ai-adj-issues/">AI-Adjacent Issues</a>
          when the problem appears tied to runtime, tools, product surface,
          permissions, workspace state, memory, configuration, or environment
          differences.
        </p>

        <p>
          Use <a href="/workbench/search/">Search</a> when you already know what
          you are looking for.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
